-- title:
--   Pointwise recognition of π(U_q) in the localised Hecke algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, let $p$ be a prime with $p\neq 2$ and $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$ (a two-dimensional $k$-space $V$ with a monoid map $\mathrm{Gal}(\bar{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)\to\mathrm{End}_k V$ trivial on the fixed group of a finite extension of $\mathbb Q$) whose base change to $\overline{k}$ has no invariant subspace other than $0$ and everything. Let $S_0\subseteq S$ be finite sets of primes with $p\in S$, and $N\geq 1$ with every prime factor of $N$ in $S$ and outside $S_0$, $p^2\nmid N$, such that: $\bar\rho$ is unramified at each $q\in S$ with $q\neq p$, $q\nmid N$; for primes $q\neq p$ with $q\parallel N$, $\bar\rho$ is ramified at $q$ and every inertia element at $q$ has characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$; for primes $q\neq p$ with $q^2\mid N$ one has $q^3\nmid N$ and the same unipotence on inertia at $q$; and if $p\mid N$ then $\bar\rho$ is ordinary at $p$, i.e. over each valuation subring above $p$ there is a line spanned by a basis vector, stable under the decomposition group, on whose quotient inertia acts trivially. Assume weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ are spanned over $\mathbb C$ by forms with integral $q$-expansions. Let $\theta'$ be a ring homomorphism to $k$ from the Hecke algebra $\mathbb T^{S_0}$, the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S_0$) and the $U_q$ ($q$ prime, $q\mid N$, $q\notin S_0$), subject to: for primes $\ell\neq p$, $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S_0$ and any valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ over $\ell$ and any $\sigma$ which is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $P$, $\mathrm{charpoly}(\bar\rho(\sigma))=X^2-\theta'(T_\ell)X+\ell$; $\theta'(U_q)=0$ when $q^2\mid N$; and $\theta'(U_q)$ for $q\parallel N$, respectively $\theta'(T_p)$ when $p\nmid N$, $p\notin S_0$, equals the trace of any endomorphism of the inertia coinvariants $V/\sum_{\tau\in I_P}\mathrm{im}(\bar\rho(\tau)-1)$ induced by a Frobenius at that prime. Let $\theta$ be the composite of $\theta'$ with the inclusion $\mathbb T^{S}\subseteq\mathbb T^{S_0}$, let $\Psi:\mathcal T^{S}\to\mathcal T^{S_0}$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra map between the corresponding localisations [`CuspForm.heckeLocal`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) commuting with the structure maps [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.π`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L151), and let $q$ be a prime with $q\parallel N$. Suppose $u\in\mathcal T^{S}$ has the property that for every $\mathcal O$-algebra $\mathcal O'$ that is again a complete discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field, module-finite over $\mathcal O$ with local structure map, every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi:\mathcal T^{S}\to\mathcal O'$, every $M\geq 1$ dividing $N$, every newform $g$ of weight two on $\Gamma_0(M)$ (a normalised eigenform whose eigensystem away from $N$ occurs at no proper divisor of $M$), every ring homomorphism $\chi_g:\mathbb T_M^{S}\to\mathbb C$ with $\chi_g(T_\ell)=a_\ell(g)$ for primes $\ell\nmid M$, $\ell\notin S$, and every ring homomorphism $\iota$ from the image of $\chi_g$ to $\mathcal O'$ with $\iota(\chi_g(T_\ell))=\psi(\pi(T_\ell))$ for primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, one has $q\mid M$ and there is $a\in\{1,-1\}$ with $a_q(g)=a$ and $\psi(u)=a$. Then $\Psi(u)=\pi(U_q)$ in $\mathcal T^{S_0}$.
--
--   This is the step which identifies an element of the localisation of the Hecke algebra away from $S$, recognised only through its values at all arithmetic points, with the image of the Atkin–Lehner operator $U_q$ in the localisation of the larger Hecke algebra away from $S_0$; it is the guarded form, placed under the full type-$\Sigma$ hypothesis block on $N$ and $\bar\rho$ used by the comparison of the two localised Hecke algebras. It is used by [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_apply_eq_pi_U_of_not_sq_dvd_of_not_isUnramifiedAt_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_apply_eq_pi_U_of_not_sq_dvd_of_not_isUnramifiedAt_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq), in the proof that the map between the two localised Hecke algebras is bijective.
